  "narration": {
    "title": "Great Players, Bad Records, No Spotlight",
    "intro": "Not every star gets to play in October. Today we pull the best healthy players off the ten worst teams in baseball, the ones doing real work for clubs going nowhere. Houston's Yordan Alvarez headlines a list that deserves better company.",
    "gem_pitchers_lead": "Cincinnati's Chase Burns is the find here, a 2.01 ERA and 1.02 WHIP with 95 strikeouts and eight wins on a losing club. The Angels send two: Jos\u00e9 Soriano keeps runs off the board at 2.79, while Reid Detmers' 100 strikeouts lead the group despite only three wins to show for it.",
    "gem_hitters_lead": "Alvarez sits a tier above everyone at a 1.070 OPS with 24 homers and a .325 average, wasted on a 35-41 team. Juan Soto carries the Mets at .980, and Colorado's Hunter Goodman has quietly hit 21 homers in the thin air for a 28-47 Rockies side."
  }
